From 63c1a5d43667ade541f0fd408e8dc8a419bfe4b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] failover: read the database cas from labelled configmaps

kyverno copies the ca.crt of every namespace labelled bedrock.io/database
into a db-ca-<cluster> configmap in bedrock-failover. the observers, the
verifier and the checker list them by label every 30 seconds, so a new
cluster is trusted without editing the pg-ca volumes, which are gone.
a ca is public, so it travels in a configmap they can already read.
the image moves to 0.3.0: 0.2.0 still reads the old volume.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VY52wmc8bdkXpT2ZSpdNxw
